  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "q0OGU21VVa5IVOnc9SW0ViIE33Q=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:30:03.552Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The guide splits breaking changes into four types, each with its own checklist:\n\n- **Type 1 \u2014 API**: signature changes, removals, renames;\n- **Type 2 \u2014 Data**: schema changes, field modifications;\n- **Type 3 \u2014 Behavioural**: how an API works changes *without* its signature changing;\n- **Type 4 \u2014 Dependency**: major dependency upgrades, runtime requirements.\n\nEvery checklist runs the same five phases: **planning** (evaluate necessity and impact), **implementation** (build it with backward compatibility), **documentation** (migration guide, docs), **release** (roll out with communication), and **removal or enforcement** in the next major version.\n\nThe general principles are stated as rules, not preferences: breaking changes **only in `x.0.0`**; **deprecate first**; provide migration paths; give a minimum **3\u20136 month deprecation period**; keep old APIs working during deprecation; document with before/after examples in `RELEASE-NOTES.md`; and use **feature flags** to control rollout.\n\nSemantic versioning is followed strictly, with one carve-out that matters in a monorepo publishing `-dev.N` builds nightly: **pre-release versions may include breaking changes** (`1.0.0-alpha.1`, `-beta.2`, `-rc.1`), clearly labelled with the matching npm tag. So a breaking change in a `dev` build is within the rules; the same change in a published minor or patch is not \u2014 \"a hard rule with no exceptions\". Version bumps ride `@jscutlery/semver` and conventional commits, with `!` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` triggering a major.\n\n## Provenance\n- `docs/BREAKING-CHANGES-GUIDE.md` \u2014 Overview \u203a Types of Breaking Changes; General Principles; Semantic Versioning \u203a TLDR\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:30:03.552Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:30:03.552Z"
    }
  },
  {
